<version>1.0.0</version>
<language>Rust</language>
Implement src/lib.rs for physics-tools 0.1.0, using pinned serde=1.0.228,
serde_json=1.0.151 and existing qft-symbolics 0.1.0 path dependency.
This specification governs only the bounded early F12/F13 bridge. General
F09/F10 expression/proof engines and complete F13 acceptance are not implemented.
No external runtime, arbitrary execution, provider, Python, C++, shell, MCP,
proof certificate, formal proof, numeric fallback or PASS status is allowed.

Public interface: INPUT_LIMIT=1048576, MAX_LABELS=12, MAX_LABEL_BYTES=64,
MAX_PAIRINGS=10395, DOMAIN="formal_symmetric_h"; Outcome has response:
serde_json::Value and exit_code:u8. Export error(status,code,message,exit_code),
discovery()->Value, pairing_cost(usize)->Option<u64>,
handle_bytes(&[u8])->Outcome and handle_reader(impl std::io::Read)->Outcome.

One request object with command:string; optional labels:Vec<String>,
domain:String, budget:u64. Strict serde typed object MUST deny unknown fields,
duplicate fields (including null first occurrences), extra JSON, invalid UTF8,
wrong types and nesting. All parsing failures produce invalid_input/malformed_json.
Discovery accepts exactly {"command":"discover"}; any extra field, even null,
is invalid_input/discovery_fields. Unknown command is unsupported/operation.
gamma_trace requires all three labels/domain/budget, otherwise invalid_input/
missing_fields. Empty/whitespace domain invalid_input/empty_domain; other than
formal_symmetric_h unsupported/domain. Labels may form an empty word; otherwise
<=12 labels each 1..64 ASCII bytes matching [A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*.
Too many labels over_budget/word_length; bad labels invalid_input/label.
Budget zero invalid_input/zero_budget; budget >10395 or less than pairing cost
is over_budget/pairing_budget. Cost=1 for empty/odd words, (n-1)!! for positive
even words, checked multiplication and None for n>12. Bounds apply before kernel.

Call existing qft_symbolics::clifford::trace on caller labels, never a fixed
lookup. Entire trace AND serialization MUST catch unwinding kernel panic as
inconclusive/kernel_panic (no success evidence). Leave default panic hook so
stderr may have diagnostics. OOM, abort and OS failures are outside this boundary.
Exact trace has integral real coefficients. Serialize canonical kernel display
as structured polynomial terms: coefficient is signed decimal integer string,
factors array contains exact h(byte_length:label;byte_length:label) variable
strings. Zero polynomial empty terms. Retain display string for audit. Do not
access private kernel data or modify kernel; unexpected display format must
become inconclusive, never an invented result.

Responses carry schema_version physics-tools.v1, status, formal_proof=false,
evidence_kind exact_algebra only for computed, null otherwise. Success carries
result; failure carries error:{code,message}. Exit 0 for discovered/computed,
2 invalid_input, 3 unsupported, 4 over_budget, 5 inconclusive. No PASS.
Computed result carries operation gamma_trace, exact input labels, domain,
backend qft-symbolics 0.1.0, arithmetic checked_i128_exact, budget and pairing_bound,
polynomial coefficient/factor encoding, display, terms, and explicit assumptions:
four-component trace without gamma5; symmetric formal h; anticommutator=2h;
h=-eta in Srednicki eta=(-,+,+,+); trace identity=4; labels free and never
summed. Repeated labels mean same formal slot, not normalized diagonal entries,
dimension contractions or an Einstein sum. Unknown domains unsupported.

Discovery MUST enumerate discover and gamma_trace only; native_rust runtime,
CLI stdin/stdout transport, no MCP; request schema and strict field behavior,
all limits/statuses/exit codes; checked-i128 intermediates, polynomial term
limit8192/degree64, unwind inconclusive; conventions and all capability limits.
The 12-distinct-label pairing count can exceed kernel term limit: explicitly
retain kernel bound rather than promising every length12 input computes.
Read at most INPUT_LIMIT+1 bytes using Read::take; >limit is over_budget/input_limit;
I/O failure invalid_input/input_io. Do not echo malformed bytes or panic payloads.
Keep independent tests/test_lib.rs outside generated output. Verify 0/2/4 formulas,
explicit matrix cases, new labels, repeated-label assumptions, strict parser,
resource boundaries and injected panic behind actual production guard.
Manual agent implementation is authorized; automated regeneration is pending.
